WEBVTT

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:06.860
If there's no reason for your kindness, 
are you just doing this on a whim?

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:10.920
I wanted to become friends 
with the two of you,

00:00:11.350 --> 00:00:14.490
but this is no different from being your pet.

00:00:15.310 --> 00:00:19.240
I'm a human! I'm not some companion animal!

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:32.420
<b>Trapped in</b>

00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:34.760
<b>a Dating Sim</b>

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:39.390
<b>Trapped in
a Dating Sim</b>

00:01:55.530 --> 00:02:00.550
She's a Doormat

00:01:59.210 --> 00:02:01.010
A pet, huh?

00:02:01.460 --> 00:02:04.440
She's probably feeling dejected 
because she had such intense malice

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:06.420
directed toward her at the academy.

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:08.640
I don't think you need to worry about it.

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:11.140
I can't <i>not</i> worry.

00:02:11.140 --> 00:02:14.430
I've got a heart as delicate as glass.

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:18.570
Your heart is made of 
bulletproof glass, Master.

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:21.640
Well, it's for the best.

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:25.860
I got ahead of myself and got involved with 
the protagonist and rich girl antagonist,

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:27.080
and now I'm paying for it.

00:02:27.330 --> 00:02:32.490
In this case, I believe the cause 
was you preventing Olivia's growth.

00:02:32.490 --> 00:02:35.490
I prevented her growth? Don't be ridiculous.

00:02:35.490 --> 00:02:37.840
I've helped her in all kinds of ways.

00:02:38.130 --> 00:02:42.700
And that's preventing Olivia's mental growth.

00:02:44.470 --> 00:02:48.410
I'm sure Olivia made a very cute pet.

00:02:48.410 --> 00:02:52.980
After all, in this world, 
she's valuable to you as a doormat.

00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:06.560
Are you satisfied?

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:10.260
I wish I could hit you again, 
but my hand hurts now.

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:18.510
Ugh.

00:03:18.860 --> 00:03:22.430
Man, you look at me like you really hate me.

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:26.240
Practicing your sword skills?

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:27.690
Yeah, that's right.

00:03:28.830 --> 00:03:30.890
Why don't you practice your magic?

00:03:30.890 --> 00:03:32.770
Isn't magic your specialty?

00:03:33.110 --> 00:03:37.260
I know that. I'm doing this 
so I can defeat you someday.

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:39.780
We've decided to work hard until that day.

00:03:40.020 --> 00:03:44.480
Are you stupid? I'm not 
fighting you guys again.

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:46.780
You'll be losers for life.

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:48.290
Wha—

00:03:53.550 --> 00:03:56.290
You have nothing to say to that?

00:03:56.510 --> 00:04:00.790
If I have time for that, I'd rather practice 
my swing as many times as possible.

00:04:02.060 --> 00:04:06.300
After all, of the five 
of us, I'm the weakest.

00:04:07.870 --> 00:04:10.310
I want Marie to look at me.

00:04:10.860 --> 00:04:14.760
When the five of us are together,
I worry I'm overshadowed by the others.

00:04:16.910 --> 00:04:19.320
Of course, I'm number one 
when it comes to appearance,

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:22.940
but I've fallen behind in other ways.

00:04:23.310 --> 00:04:26.290
<i>He just casually called 
himself the most handsome.</i>

00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:30.700
What's so great about her? 
It's not like she's that good-looki—

00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:32.520
It's not about her looks! 
It's what's on the inside!

00:04:32.520 --> 00:04:34.650
Well, she's terrible on the inside, too!

00:04:37.900 --> 00:04:42.420
Wh-What is this hunk of metal 
wandering around your ship?

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:44.430
But this is a good opportunity.

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:48.930
Let us fight, Bartfort!

00:04:49.230 --> 00:04:51.180
No way. It's too cold out.

00:04:51.470 --> 00:04:52.430
Don't waste your breath!

00:04:55.890 --> 00:04:58.910
Why do you want to challenge me to 
a type of fight you're not good at?

00:04:58.910 --> 00:04:59.650
Are you stupid?

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:02.360
My academic grades are better than yours!

00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:04.900
I want to be proud of who 
I am when I face Marie!

00:05:06.060 --> 00:05:09.910
<i>These guys are doing their best 
to face Marie their own way.</i>

00:05:11.260 --> 00:05:13.470
<i>In contrast, I'm...</i>

00:05:17.540 --> 00:05:19.500
Now I'll press the attack!

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:25.670
Ow.

00:05:25.670 --> 00:05:27.950
You've gotta be stupid.

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:30.930
I thought I could do it.

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:32.680
Maybe after another decade of training.

00:05:32.680 --> 00:05:36.450
Next time, I swear I will defeat you!

00:05:42.040 --> 00:05:43.950
That looked fun.

00:05:43.950 --> 00:05:47.300
You sent that robot out here 
with wooden swords, didn't you?

00:05:47.300 --> 00:05:48.320
Yes.

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:52.600
They sure are putting a lot 
of thought into things.

00:05:54.810 --> 00:05:57.270
All for that good-for-nothing girl, though.

00:06:07.930 --> 00:06:09.810
This is why I didn't want to come here!

00:06:09.810 --> 00:06:12.340
This dungeon's monsters are strong!

00:06:12.340 --> 00:06:14.100
Don't give up!

00:06:14.420 --> 00:06:19.230
There's a bright future 
waiting for us up ahead!

00:06:19.230 --> 00:06:23.730
<i>I need to do whatever it takes to retrieve 
that item before the protagonist does.</i>

00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:28.580
It's not like I can count on Prince Julius!

00:06:33.890 --> 00:06:35.490
I've come up with an idea, Jilk.

00:06:35.860 --> 00:06:37.820
What do you think of 
sneaking out of the palace

00:06:37.820 --> 00:06:40.370
and meeting up with Greg and Brad?

00:06:40.370 --> 00:06:43.500
A fine idea. I am impressed, Your Highness.

00:06:44.490 --> 00:06:47.070
But how should we escape?

00:06:48.270 --> 00:06:49.880
I've got an idea, Jilk.

00:06:49.880 --> 00:06:51.390
Most impressive, Your Highness.

00:06:51.390 --> 00:06:54.280
We'll wear masks. We should get cloaks, too.

00:06:54.280 --> 00:06:57.920
I see. We'll disguises ourselves and escape.

00:06:57.920 --> 00:06:59.770
But how shall we make the 
necessary arrangements?

00:07:01.720 --> 00:07:03.260
I've got an idea, Jilk.

00:07:03.260 --> 00:07:05.020
Most impressive, Your Highness.

00:07:05.020 --> 00:07:06.060
What?

00:07:06.060 --> 00:07:08.990
<i>Budget request for cloaks and masks.</i>

00:07:08.990 --> 00:07:11.030
<i>Purpose: entertainment.</i>

00:07:11.450 --> 00:07:13.930
What were they thinking, submitting a request

00:07:13.930 --> 00:07:17.160
for a disguise to the royal palace itself?

00:07:17.420 --> 00:07:21.070
Perhaps those boys really 
are stupid after all.

00:07:22.030 --> 00:07:24.260
Your budget request has been denied.

00:07:37.250 --> 00:07:39.310
Ugh, a sausage fest first 
thing in the morning.

00:07:39.530 --> 00:07:43.390
It's not like I want to see your face 
first thing in the morning, either.

00:07:43.390 --> 00:07:46.160
More importantly, what are we 
going to do about the sky pirates?

00:07:46.160 --> 00:07:48.320
The main force is still out there, isn't it?

00:07:50.390 --> 00:07:54.320
<i>In the game, they can be left alone 
until midway through the second year.</i>

00:07:55.190 --> 00:07:59.200
<i>But this is an opportunity to 
acquire the Holy Necklace...</i>

00:07:59.650 --> 00:08:02.850
We've located the pirates' hideout.

00:08:03.160 --> 00:08:05.190
If we wait a bit longer before going in—

00:08:06.650 --> 00:08:10.960
Master, it seems the pirates 
have decided to attack first.

00:08:11.620 --> 00:08:13.590
They acted faster than I expected.

00:08:13.980 --> 00:08:15.590
Is it the pirates?

00:08:16.010 --> 00:08:17.780
Yeah, looks like it.

00:08:18.470 --> 00:08:19.970
We'll fight, too.

00:08:19.970 --> 00:08:22.100
Let me borrow an Armor,
even if it's falling apart!

00:08:22.340 --> 00:08:26.360
Me, too. I found something that looked 
usable among the pirates' Armor.

00:08:26.680 --> 00:08:27.870
Please!

00:08:27.870 --> 00:08:30.850
No. You need to consider your own posit—

00:08:32.750 --> 00:08:34.990
We know we'd be holding you back,

00:08:34.990 --> 00:08:37.320
but we can't just sit by and watch.

00:08:37.320 --> 00:08:38.990
We want to fight, too.

00:08:39.390 --> 00:08:40.780
Bartfort!

00:08:44.090 --> 00:08:46.660
Let me check the Armor first.

00:08:46.660 --> 00:08:48.320
After that, you can do whatever you want.

00:08:52.820 --> 00:08:56.520
<i>Why did I say those awful things to him?</i>

00:08:57.950 --> 00:09:00.740
<i>Mr. Leon helped me.</i>

00:09:01.180 --> 00:09:05.340
<i>Just getting to be by his side was a miracle.</i>

00:09:06.330 --> 00:09:10.190
<i>I'm the one who selfishly 
sought more than that.</i>

00:09:10.870 --> 00:09:11.990
Why?

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:16.200
Wh-What was that?

00:09:24.650 --> 00:09:25.780
A barrier?

00:09:32.570 --> 00:09:33.710
Mr. Leon!

00:09:37.930 --> 00:09:39.030
What a pain.

00:09:42.890 --> 00:09:44.900
All right. That just leaves...

00:09:47.970 --> 00:09:49.150
Damn it!

00:09:53.400 --> 00:09:55.900
P-Please let me through!

00:09:58.780 --> 00:09:59.660
Let me through!

00:10:04.140 --> 00:10:05.430
<i>Mr. Leon!</i>

00:10:15.310 --> 00:10:16.410
Huh?

00:10:24.130 --> 00:10:25.940
What is this trash?

00:10:28.260 --> 00:10:30.440
You're a pretty girl, aren't you?

00:10:32.190 --> 00:10:34.190
No, you don't!

00:10:36.190 --> 00:10:37.690
Wh-Who are you?

00:10:37.690 --> 00:10:39.950
It's Brad! Flee, quickly!

00:10:40.330 --> 00:10:44.710
You bastard. A brat like 
you shouldn't get too cocky!

00:10:47.530 --> 00:10:48.580
Mr. Brad!

00:10:53.050 --> 00:10:54.090
It's so hard!

00:10:55.090 --> 00:10:59.090
I've been through far worse 
shit than you have, kid!

00:11:03.830 --> 00:11:05.870
Out of the way!

00:11:06.190 --> 00:11:07.850
I-Is he a monster?

00:11:07.850 --> 00:11:09.350
Who is this guy?

00:11:09.610 --> 00:11:12.070
Don't kill them! Capture them all!

00:11:12.070 --> 00:11:15.860
That's an absurd request. 
You're struggling because of that.

00:11:15.860 --> 00:11:20.740
The guy who blew me away earlier 
was probably the pirate boss.

00:11:20.740 --> 00:11:22.730
If we can just do something about him...

00:11:25.740 --> 00:11:26.960
Take this!

00:11:26.960 --> 00:11:28.250
Die!

00:11:28.580 --> 00:11:31.130
Master, your reaction speed has decreased.

00:11:31.130 --> 00:11:34.250
Your operation technique and other 
capabilities have deteriorated, as well.

00:11:34.250 --> 00:11:36.820
Yeah, well, sorry I haven't practiced enough!

00:11:36.820 --> 00:11:39.410
Actually, I believe it is a mental problem.

00:11:39.410 --> 00:11:40.380
Shut up!

00:11:40.840 --> 00:11:41.880
You little...

00:11:44.030 --> 00:11:47.990
Master, I have confirmed the 
pirate boss is on the deck.

00:11:47.990 --> 00:11:49.390
Olivia is in danger.

00:11:49.990 --> 00:11:52.520
Livia? Why'd you let her outside?!

00:11:52.840 --> 00:11:57.480
I am sorry. It would seem the work 
robots shut down temporarily.

00:11:57.480 --> 00:12:00.030
Something must have disabled them.

00:12:00.030 --> 00:12:01.650
Damn it!

00:12:04.520 --> 00:12:05.530
Master.

00:12:06.590 --> 00:12:09.040
Allowing them to join the battle 
was the right choice.

00:12:09.630 --> 00:12:12.790
They are fighting to protect Olivia.

00:12:13.160 --> 00:12:14.570
Let's go, Brad.

00:12:14.570 --> 00:12:16.040
Ready when you are.

00:12:19.920 --> 00:12:23.620
Yeah. This is how it should be.

00:12:24.680 --> 00:12:29.660
<i>The protagonist belongs with the 
handsome romantic interests.</i>

00:12:29.660 --> 00:12:32.430
<i>I don't belong at Livia's side.</i>

00:12:33.870 --> 00:12:35.780
<i>After all, I'm a mob character.</i>

00:12:37.720 --> 00:12:42.690
<i>But I have my own role to play.</i>

00:12:42.690 --> 00:12:45.950
Increase power output. 
We'll use number three.

00:12:45.950 --> 00:12:47.550
I'll crush them.

00:12:55.110 --> 00:12:57.340
D-Damn...

00:12:57.340 --> 00:12:59.210
So this is the end...

00:12:59.700 --> 00:13:01.590
You guys were a pain in the ass.

00:13:02.810 --> 00:13:05.340
Come here, girl.

00:13:05.730 --> 00:13:08.950
If you run, I'll kill these two.

00:13:09.950 --> 00:13:12.430
<i>Th-This is my fault.</i>

00:13:12.860 --> 00:13:14.900
<i>I'm a burden. I'm useless.</i>

00:13:15.260 --> 00:13:17.600
<i>All I do is cause trouble for everyone else.</i>

00:13:18.730 --> 00:13:19.750
<i>I...</i>

00:13:50.590 --> 00:13:54.520
S-Spare me! I surrender! I surrender!

00:13:54.520 --> 00:13:57.140
Surrender? Come on, now.

00:13:57.140 --> 00:14:00.570
You're a famous pirate. That's no fun.

00:14:00.570 --> 00:14:03.020
Try fighting back until the end.

00:14:05.960 --> 00:14:08.280
Come on, fight back!

00:14:08.570 --> 00:14:12.780
S-Spare me! Please spare me!

00:14:13.670 --> 00:14:15.810
M-Mr. Leon, don't!

00:14:16.120 --> 00:14:19.430
Don't you think you're asking too 
much after all the havoc you wrought?

00:14:19.430 --> 00:14:23.570
Why don't you tell your 
subordinates to surrender first?

00:14:25.120 --> 00:14:26.760
Hey, found it.

00:14:28.550 --> 00:14:31.300
G-Give that back! That's important!

00:14:31.300 --> 00:14:35.430
I don't care. If you've got a 
problem, come and get it.

00:14:46.990 --> 00:14:48.270
<i>Mr. Leon...</i>

00:14:55.490 --> 00:14:57.010
It's over.

00:15:00.190 --> 00:15:01.460
Mr. Brad!

00:15:01.690 --> 00:15:03.240
I'll heal you right away.

00:15:03.240 --> 00:15:05.000
Th-Thank you.

00:15:05.000 --> 00:15:07.710
Don't thank me. You were hurt because of me.

00:15:07.710 --> 00:15:11.910
You're wrong about that. 
We're trying to become knights.

00:15:11.910 --> 00:15:15.150
A knight should be kind to women—ow!

00:15:17.250 --> 00:15:20.100
You're skilled in the same magics as Marie.

00:15:20.400 --> 00:15:22.690
Ms. Marie is skilled in healing magic, too?

00:15:22.690 --> 00:15:25.590
Yeah, she's our goddess.

00:15:25.590 --> 00:15:30.740
With Marie around, no injury 
is ever... too... much...

00:15:31.430 --> 00:15:32.600
Mr. Brad?

00:15:35.950 --> 00:15:37.120
You make a good couple.

00:15:37.350 --> 00:15:38.620
Huh?

00:15:39.500 --> 00:15:44.630
I guess everything's made to end 
up where it belongs after all.

00:15:46.060 --> 00:15:47.630
Mr. Leon?

00:15:49.030 --> 00:15:51.320
Greg, you're pretty strong.

00:15:51.320 --> 00:15:54.500
Are you being sarcastic? 
More importantly, I'm sorry.

00:15:54.500 --> 00:15:56.890
I broke the Armor we acquired.

00:15:57.220 --> 00:16:00.050
What you did was more than worth it.

00:16:00.050 --> 00:16:02.690
I'm going to bring Brad inside. 
Will you help me carry him?

00:16:02.690 --> 00:16:03.900
He got hurt?

00:16:04.200 --> 00:16:07.310
He's all right. Ms. Olivia healed him.

00:16:12.210 --> 00:16:16.270
<i>Mr. Leon, why?</i>

00:16:26.920 --> 00:16:30.980
<i>Please call me Livia.</i>

00:16:37.540 --> 00:16:39.430
They'd amassed all this treasure, huh?

00:16:40.120 --> 00:16:42.140
Well, they were pirates.

00:16:42.510 --> 00:16:45.560
I doubt we can expect a reward 
from the Wayne family,

00:16:47.030 --> 00:16:50.710
but I believe we will also receive 
the bounty from the palace.

00:16:51.060 --> 00:16:53.570
I'm thankful for that,

00:16:54.130 --> 00:16:56.280
but were you able to find 
evidence linking the pirates

00:16:56.280 --> 00:17:00.200
to Count Offrey's family and Stephanie, 
who orchestrated this mess?

00:17:00.590 --> 00:17:04.710
Yes. I discovered documents 
of their correspondence.

00:17:04.710 --> 00:17:08.210
Good. That'll get rid of the trash.

00:17:08.650 --> 00:17:10.700
The kingdom will improve slightly.

00:17:11.220 --> 00:17:13.950
Actually, I guess the entire 
kingdom itself is trash.

00:17:13.950 --> 00:17:18.900
I would not hesitate to destroy 
this kingdom and this world.

00:17:18.900 --> 00:17:23.940
After destroying it, it would be possible 
for me to create a world that suits you.

00:17:23.940 --> 00:17:26.600
Sounds nice. Maybe I'll assemble a harem,

00:17:27.020 --> 00:17:30.490
with elves and cat-eared beast women.

00:17:32.250 --> 00:17:37.660
I guess my thinking is no different 
from the academy girls', huh?

00:17:37.970 --> 00:17:40.210
I'm glad you have your answer.

00:17:40.550 --> 00:17:43.500
Do you feel better now that you've taken 
out your frustrations on the pirates?

00:17:43.810 --> 00:17:47.370
It's not that Olivia hates you now.

00:17:47.370 --> 00:17:50.160
She's just become emotionally unstable.

00:17:50.160 --> 00:17:51.750
I know.

00:17:57.530 --> 00:18:01.260
It's just time for me to go back 
to being a proper mob character.

00:18:04.780 --> 00:18:09.490
Master, there's a Redgrave 
airship headed our way.

00:18:12.350 --> 00:18:15.180
Ms. Angelica must've pulled some strings.

00:18:15.580 --> 00:18:17.430
Let's let them handle the rest.

00:18:18.970 --> 00:18:20.870
What's the meaning of this?!

00:18:21.290 --> 00:18:23.730
Ow, my wound.

00:18:23.730 --> 00:18:26.210
We aren't the ones who defeated the pirates.

00:18:26.210 --> 00:18:28.040
We can't accept this reward.

00:18:28.040 --> 00:18:31.490
Are you telling us to take credit 
for Bartfort's achievement?

00:18:31.490 --> 00:18:39.800
You must accept. Baron Bartfort reported 
that he simply assisted the two of you.

00:18:39.800 --> 00:18:40.440
What?

00:18:40.440 --> 00:18:41.680
What does that mean?

00:18:42.440 --> 00:18:44.760
I was told not to say anything,

00:18:44.760 --> 00:18:48.690
but the baron has made an 
appeal to both your families.

00:18:48.690 --> 00:18:53.130
He's asked them to reconsider your 
disinheritance in light of your exploits.

00:18:56.750 --> 00:18:58.570
Are you sure this is what you wanted?

00:18:59.230 --> 00:19:03.850
It'd be good for me to 
see those two reinstated.

00:19:04.250 --> 00:19:06.830
They seem like they'd protect Ms. Olivia.

00:19:06.830 --> 00:19:12.080
There's the matter of Brad and Greg, 
but there's also the Offrey family's daughter.

00:19:12.670 --> 00:19:14.590
Stephanie, huh?

00:19:15.260 --> 00:19:18.840
We can let the royal palace and 
the Redgrave family handle her.

00:19:20.550 --> 00:19:25.230
They'll inflict a far worse 
punishment than I ever could.

00:19:27.210 --> 00:19:29.780
If you're satisfied, then I'm fine with that.

00:19:29.780 --> 00:19:32.850
However, Angelica was upset with you.

00:19:33.150 --> 00:19:35.700
She wanted to know why you made Olivia cry.

00:19:35.700 --> 00:19:38.020
Huh? Oh.

00:19:44.470 --> 00:19:46.920
Rich girls can be so fussy.

00:19:46.920 --> 00:19:49.540
Do you intend to distance 
yourself from Angelica, as well?

00:19:49.950 --> 00:19:55.500
Yeah. If anything, we've 
been too close until now.

00:20:12.030 --> 00:20:16.610
<i>Will our relationship ever be the same again?</i>

00:20:20.780 --> 00:20:23.320
Your Highness, we've made a decision.

00:20:23.320 --> 00:20:26.070
A decision? About what?

00:20:26.070 --> 00:20:28.990
We want to beat Bartfort as fellow men.

00:20:28.990 --> 00:20:33.090
He's an incredible knight, 
but someday we'll catch up to him.

00:20:33.900 --> 00:20:35.580
Guys...

00:20:35.930 --> 00:20:39.340
Your Highness, would it be 
possible to see the queen?

00:20:39.340 --> 00:20:43.590
We wouldn't be men if we didn't 
return the favor we owe him.

00:20:45.320 --> 00:20:48.220
Brad, Greg...

00:20:48.990 --> 00:20:52.230
Do you guys really hate me that much?

00:20:52.630 --> 00:20:55.320
You've been promoted from upper 
sixth to lower fifth rank.

00:20:55.320 --> 00:20:58.550
Those two must have talked 
to the palace for you.

00:20:58.550 --> 00:21:00.730
There's no way this is acceptable!

00:21:01.200 --> 00:21:03.650
That's two ranks higher than my own father!

00:21:03.650 --> 00:21:06.930
Also, you received this letter.

00:21:07.820 --> 00:21:09.140
A letter?

00:21:10.100 --> 00:21:14.150
The Atlee family? So it's 
from Clarice's family.

00:21:15.100 --> 00:21:17.850
<i>Dear Baron Bartfort.</i>

00:21:17.850 --> 00:21:20.430
<i>Thank you for helping my daughter.</i>

00:21:20.430 --> 00:21:25.010
<i>As a token of my appreciation, I'd like 
you to accept an air bike as thanks.</i>

00:21:25.010 --> 00:21:27.470
<i>Also, though this may be impertinent of me,</i>

00:21:27.470 --> 00:21:31.880
<i>I have recommended you be promoted to 
upper fifth rank after your graduation.</i>

00:21:37.520 --> 00:21:42.510
Congratulations. You'll be 
promoted once you graduate.

00:21:42.510 --> 00:21:46.530
P-Please, no more! I'm going 
on a trip somewhere!

00:21:46.760 --> 00:21:49.250
You can't. Classes start tomorrow.

00:21:55.120 --> 00:21:57.790
<b>Trapped in a Dating Sim</b>

00:23:26.190 --> 00:23:29.260
You travel abroad every year for your 
school trip? Nobles sure are something.

00:23:29.260 --> 00:23:31.180
It's an opportunity to gain 
knowledge and friends.

00:23:31.180 --> 00:23:32.550
I don't understand it.

00:23:32.550 --> 00:23:35.430
Next time, "Unlike You Wannabe Nobles."

00:23:35.430 --> 00:23:37.480
That's because you're not very aristocratic.

00:23:37.480 --> 00:23:39.020
Neither are you, Mr. Disinherited.
